{"id":43605,"ord":1,"n_segments":210,"prev":43604,"next":43606,"doc":{"id":"52240","title":"52240_Frank _Machito_ Grillo oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Frank \"Machito\" Grillo","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/52240/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=52240"},"chapter":"Opening and Havana childhood","title":"Birth date, parents, siblings and ancestry","category":"family_childhood","summary":"Machito gives his birth (1908), his parents Martha and Rogelio, five siblings, and the African and Spanish ancestry of his grandparents.","period":"1908","year_from":1908,"year_to":1908,"words":148,"start":[2,1],"end":[3,0],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=52240#s43605","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[]},"people":[{"name":"Anisa","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Estela","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Graciela Perez","qid":"Q5591543","n":1},{"name":"Rogelio, Jr.","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Martha","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Rogelio (Machito's father)","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Martha (Machito's mother)","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":47,"theme_name":"Growing up and learning music: family, first instruments, teachers","community":117,"community_name":"Where I came from: parents, siblings and birth","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":2,"b":1,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"When were you born?"},{"p":2,"b":2,"s":"MACHITO","x":"The truth?"},{"p":2,"b":3,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"The truth."},{"p":2,"b":4,"s":"MACHITO","x":"1908"},{"p":2,"b":5,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"Okay, the date and the year?"},{"p":2,"b":6,"s":"MACHITO","x":"'The year is 16th February 1930 - uh - 1908."},{"p":2,"b":7,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"Okay, and what was your mother and father's name?"},{"p":2,"b":8,"s":"MACHITO","x":"Well, Martha and Rogelio."},{"p":2,"b":9,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"Okay, how many children did your family have?"},{"p":2,"b":10,"s":"MACHITO","x":"Six"},{"p":2,"b":11,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"What were their names?"},{"p":2,"b":12,"s":"MACHITO","x":"Uhh - Anisa; - it was after me ...."},{"p":2,"b":13,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"You were the first born in the family?"},{"p":2,"b":14,"s":"MACHITO","x":"Yes"},{"p":2,"b":15,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"Okay, go ahead."},{"p":2,"b":16,"s":"MACHITO","x":"... Anisa, Estela, Graciela, ahh Marta y Rogelio."},{"p":2,"b":17,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"Okay, as far as you know, what is the nationality makeup on your father's side?"},{"p":2,"b":18,"s":"MACHITO","x":"Well, my father and mother were Cuban."},{"p":2,"b":19,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"Uh - huh?"},{"p":2,"b":20,"s":"MACHITO","x":"Yes"},{"p":2,"b":21,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"And their ancestry?"},{"p":2,"b":22,"s":"MACHITO","x":"Ahh from my mother's side there was a black African and a Spanish person, you know, my grandfather was Spanish."},{"p":2,"b":23,"s":"MR. SALAZAR","x":"And on your father's side?"},{"p":3,"b":0,"s":"MACHITO","x":"On my father side my grandmother was a mulata and my grandfather was black."}]}